{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01CGJMrF4Wx6FEBanBCRMXwm","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t{\"result\":\"{\\\"success\\\": true, \\\"data\\\": {\\\"path\\\": \\\"/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0509_9/projects/event-gated-adaptive-horizon/literature_map.yaml\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"# Literature Map — event-gated-adaptive-horizon\\\\n# Last updated: 2026-05-15\\\\n# Total: 76 papers (72 existing + 4 incremental scan 2026-05-15)\\\\n\\\\n# ============================================================\\\\n# EXISTING CITATIONS (already in paper.tex)\\\\n# ============================================================\\\\n\\\\n- paper_id: sutton1999options\\\\n  title: \\\\\\\"Between MDPs and Semi-MDPs: A Framework for Temporal Abstraction in Reinforcement Learning\\\\\\\"\\\\n  authors: [Sutton R.S., Precup D., Singh S.]\\\\n  year: 1999\\\\n  venue: \\\\\\\"Artificial Intelligence 112(1-2):181-211\\\\\\\"\\\\n  category: background\\\\n  role: \\\\\\\"Foundational options framework for temporal abstraction in RL; our work investigates why temporal abstraction fails in world-model RL\\\\\\\"\\\\n  relevance_score: 5\\\\n\\\\n- paper_id: hafner2020dreamerv1\\\\n  title: \\\\\\\"Dream to Control: Learning Behaviors by Latent Imagination\\\\\\\"\\\\n  authors: [Hafner D., Lillicrap T., Ba J., Norouzi M.]\\\\n  year: 2020\\\\n  venue: ICLR\\\\n  category: background\\\\n  role: \\\\\\\"DreamerV1 — base architecture family; our experiments build on the RSSM and imagination-based training paradigm\\\\\\\"\\\\n  relevance_score: 5\\\\n\\\\n- paper_id: hafner2023dreamerv3\\\\n  title: \\\\\\\"Mastering Diverse Domains through World Models\\\\\\\"\\\\n  authors: [Hafner D., Pasukonis J., Ba J., Lillicrap T.]\\\\n  year: 2023\\\\n  venue: \\\\\\\"arXiv:2301.04104 (Nature 2025)\\\\\\\"\\\\n  category: background\\\\n  role: \\\\\\\"DreamerV3 — the specific base system we modify; symlog transforms, discrete latents, all default hyperparameters come from here\\\\\\\"\\\\n  relevance_score: 5\\\\n\\\\n- paper_id: sharma2017figar\\\\n  title: \\\\\\\"Fine Grained Action Repetition for Deep Reinforcement Learning\\\\\\\"\\\\n  authors: [Sharma S., Lakshminarayanan A.S., Ravindran B.]\\\\n  year: 2017\\\\n  venue: \\\\\\\"ICLR Workshop\\\\\\\"\\\\n  category: method-component\\\\n  role: \\\\\\\"FiGAR — learns action-repeat durations in model-free RL; we extend the idea to imagination step size in world-model RL\\\\\\\"\\\\n  relevance_score: 4\\\\n\\\\n- paper_id: janner2019mbpo\\\\n  title: \\\\\\\"When to Trust Your Model: Model-Based Policy Optimization\\\\\\\"\\\\n  authors: [Janner M., Fu J., Zhang M., Levine S.]\\\\n  year: 2019\\\\n  venue: NeurIPS\\\\n  category: background\\\\n  role: \\\\\\\"MBPO — formalizes model exploitation in MBRL; our conditioning-induced value overestimation (CIVO) is a specific instance of model exploitation tied to temporal embedding\\\\\\\"\\\\n  relevance_score: 5\\\\n\\\\n# ============================================================\\\\n# NEW: Multi-step prediction error compounding\\\\n# ============================================================\\\\n\\\\n- paper_id: ke2019learning\\\\n  title: \\\\\\\"Learning Dynamics Model in Reinforcement Learning by Incorporating the Long Term Future\\\\\\\"\\\\n  authors: [Ke N.R., Singh A., Touati A., Goyal A., Bengio Y., Parikh D., Batra D.]\\\\n  year: 2019\\\\n  venue: ICLR\\\\n  category: background\\\\n  role: \\\\\\\"Addresses long-term dynamics prediction via latent-variable autoregressive model; directly relevant to our finding that multi-step RSSM predictions degrade with dt>1\\\\\\\"\\\\n  relevance_score: 4\\\\n\\\\n- paper_id: asadi2019combating\\\\n  title: \\\\\\\"Combating the Compounding-Error Problem with a Multi-step Model\\\\\\\"\\\\n  authors: [Asadi K., Misra D., Kim S., Littman M.L.]\\\\n  year: 2019\\\\n  venue: \\\\\\\"arXiv:1905.13320\\\\\\\"\\\\n  category: background\\\\n  role: \\\\\\\"Proposes multi-step models to bypass compounding error; our work shows that even with multi-step imagination, the dt-embedding creates a different failure mode (value overestimation) distinct from compounding error\\\\\\\"\\\\n  relevance_score: 4\\\\n\\\\n- paper_id: venkatraman2015improving\\\\n  title: \\\\\\\"Improving Multi-Step Prediction of Learned Time Series Models\\\\\\\"\\\\n  authors: [Venkatraman A., Hebert M., Bagnell J.A.]\\\\n  year: 2015\\\\n  venue: AAAI\\\\n  category: background\\\\n  role: \\\\\\\"Data-as-Demonstrator (DaD) for robust multi-step prediction; establishes theoretical guarantee relating training error to multi-step prediction error\\\\\\\"\\\\n  relevance_score: 3\\\\n\\\\n- paper_id: lambert2022investigating\\\\n  title: \\\\\\\"Investigating Compounding Prediction Errors in Learned Dynamics Models\\\\\\\"\\\\n  authors: [Lambert N., Pister K.S.J., Calandra R.]\\\\n  year: 2022\\\\n  venue: \\\\\\\"arXiv:2203.09637\\\\\\\"\\\\n  category: background\\\\n  role: \\\\\\\"Empirical study of compounding error properties; we rule out compounding error as the primary failure mechanism (008c vs 008a comparison) and identify value overestimation instead\\\\\\\"\\\\n  relevance_score: 3\\\\n\\\\n# ============================================================\\\\n# NEW: Model-predictive control with learned dynamics\\\\n# ============================================================\\\\n\\\\n- paper_id: chua2018pets\\\\n  title: \\\\\\\"Deep Reinforcement Learning in a Handful of Trials using Probabilistic Dynamics Models\\\\\\\"\\\\n  authors: [Chua K., Calandra R., McAllister R., Levine S.]\\\\n  year: 2018\\\\n  venue: NeurIPS\\\\n  category: background\\\\n  role: \\\\\\\"PETS — ensemble-based uncertainty-aware MPC; uses explicit uncertainty quantification to avoid model exploitation, contrasting with DreamerV3's implicit approach\\\\\\\"\\\\n  relevance_score: 3\\\\n\\\\n- paper_id: nagabandi2018neural\\\\n  title: \\\\\\\"Neural Network Dynamics for Model-Based Deep Reinforcement Learning with Model-Free Fine-Tuning\\\\\\\"\\\\n  authors: [Nagabandi A., Kahn G., Fearing R.S., Levine S.]\\\\n  year: 2018\\\\n  venue: ICRA\\\\n  category: background\\\\n  role: \\\\\\\"Demonstrates NN dynamics + MPC for locomotion; model errors accumulate over prediction horizon, motivating our investigation of horizon-dependent failures\\\\\\\"\\\\n  relevance_score: 3\\\\n\\\\n- paper_id: hansen2024tdmpc2\\\\n  title: \\\\\\\"TD-MPC2: Scalable, Robust World Models for Continuous Control\\\\\\\"\\\\n  authors: [Hansen N., Su H., Wang X.]\\\\n  year: 2024\\\\n  venue: \\\\\\\"ICLR (arXiv:2310.16828)\\\\\\\"\\\\n  category: background\\\\n  role: \\\\\\\"TD-MPC2 — SOTA MPC planning route (online planning + learned dynamics); DMC benchmark leader but orthogonal to imagination-based training — reviewer defense: TD-MPC2 does online MPC rollouts at test time, we study actor-critic training via imagined rollouts (DreamerV3 paradigm), not a same-level comparison\\\\\\\"\\\\n  relevance_score: 4\\\\n\\\\n# ============================================================\\\\n# NEW: Pessimistic MBRL / model exploitation mitigation\\\\n# ============================================================\\\\n\\\\n- paper_id: yu2020mopo\\\\n  title: \\\\\\\"MOPO: Model-based Offline Policy Optimization\\\\\\\"\\\\n  authors: [Yu T., Thomas G., Yu L., Ermon S., Zou J., Levine S., Finn C., Ma T.]\\\\n  year: 2020\\\\n  venue: \\\\\\\"NeurIPS (arXiv:2005.13239)\\\\\\\"\\\\n  category: background\\\\n  role: \\\\\\\"MOPO — pessimistic MBRL via uncertainty-penalized reward (reward -= λ * model_uncertainty); generic model exploitation mitigation — reviewer defense: MOPO addresses distribution shift in offline MBRL, our dt=1 imagination restriction targets dt_embedding-induced CIVO (temporal conditioning corruption), two complementary mechanisms\\\\\\\"\\\\n  relevance_score: 4\\\\n\\\\n# ============================================================\\\\n# NEW: Value overestimation mitigation\\\\n# ============================================================\\\\n\\\\n- paper_id: thrun1993issues\\\\n  title: \\\\\\\"Issues in Using Function Approximation for Reinforcement Learning\\\\\\\"\\\\n  authors: [Thrun S., Schwartz A.]\\\\n  year: 1993\\\\n  venue: \\\\\\\"Connectionist Models Summer School\\\\\\\"\\\\n  category: background\\\\n  role: \\\\\\\"First identification of systematic value overestimation from function approximation; our CIVO extends this to model-based imagination with temporal conditioning\\\\\\\"\\\\n  relevance_score: 4\\\\n\\\\n- paper_id: vanhasselt2016double\\\\n  title: \\\\\\\"Deep Reinforcement Learning with Double Q-Learning\\\\\\\"\\\\n  authors: [van Hasselt H., Guez A., Silver D.]\\\\n  year: 2016\\\\n  venue: AAAI\\\\n  category: background\\\\n  role: \\\\\\\"Double DQN — mitigates overestimation via double estimator; our finding that trained dt-embedding enables value exploitation is a complementary overestimation mechanism in MBRL\\\\\\\"\\\\n  relevance_score: 4\\\\n\\\\n- paper_id: fujimoto2018td3\\\\n  title: \\\\\\\"Addressing Function Approximation Error in Actor-Critic Methods\\\\\\\"\\\\n  authors: [Fujimoto S., van Hoof H., Meger D.]\\\\n  year: 2018\\\\n  venue: ICML\\\\n  category: method-component\\\\n  role: \\\\\\\"TD3 — clipped double-Q to limit overestimation in actor-critic; DreamerV3 uses a single critic, making it more vulnerable to the overestimation we identify\\\\\\\"\\\\n  relevance_score: 4\\\\n\\\\n- paper_id: haarnoja2018sac\\\\n  title: \\\\\\\"Soft Actor-Critic: Off-Policy Maximum Entropy Deep Reinforcement Learning with a Stochastic Actor\\\\\\\"\\\\n  authors: [Haarnoja T., Zhou A., Abbeel P., Levine S.]\\\\n  year: 2018\\\\n  venue: ICML\\\\n  category: method-component\\\\n  role: \\\\\\\"SAC — entropy regularization implicitly mitigates overestimation; relevant contrast to DreamerV3's actor which can greedily exploit overestimated values\\\\\\\"\\\\n  relevance_score: 3\\\\n\\\\n- paper_id: lee2021sunrise\\\\n  title: \\\\\\\"SUNRISE: A Simple Unified Framework for Ensemble Learning in Deep Reinforcement Learning\\\\\\\"\\\\n  authors: [Lee K., Laskin M., Srinivas A., Abbeel P.]\\\\n  year: 2021\\\\n  venue: ICML\\\\n  category: method-component\\\\n  role: \\\\\\\"Ensemble-based uncertainty weighting for value estimation; potential mitigation for our identified CIVO mechanism\\\\\\\"\\\\n  relevance_score: 3\\\\n\\\\n# ============================================================\\\\n# NEW: Delusional bias\\\\n# ============================================================\\\\n\\\\n- paper_id: lu2018nondelusional\\\\n  title: \\\\\\\"Non-delusional Q-learning and Value-Iteration\\\\\\\"\\\\n  authors: [Lu T., Schuurmans D., Boutilier C.]\\\\n  year: 2018\\\\n  venue: NeurIPS\\\\n  category: background\\\\n  role: \\\\\\\"Formalizes delusional bias from policy-class constraints in Q-learning; we identify an analogous phenomenon where temporal conditioning enables the critic to exploit model imprecision\\\\\\\"\\\\n  relevance_score: 5\\\\n\\\\n# ============================================================\\\\n# NEW: Hierarchical RL with learned models\\\\n# ============================================================\\\\n\\\\n- paper_id: hafner2022director\\\\n  title: \\\\\\\"Deep Hierarchical Planning from Pixels\\\\\\\"\\\\n  authors: [Hafner D., Lee K.-H., Fischer I., Abbeel P.]\\\\n  year: 2022\\\\n  venue: NeurIPS\\\\n  category: direct-competitor\\\\n  role: \\\\\\\"Director — hierarchical planning in Dreamer latent space via subgoals; addresses temporal abstraction through goal hierarchy rather than variable dt\\\\\\\"\\\\n  relevance_score: 4\\\\n\\\\n- paper_id: nachum2018hiro\\\\n  title: \\\\\\\"Data-Efficient Hierarchical Reinforcement Learning\\\\\\\"\\\\n  authors: [Nachum O., Gu S., Lee H., Levine S.]\\\\n  year: 2018\\\\n  venue: NeurIPS\\\\n  category: background\\\\n  role: \\\\\\\"HIRO — off-policy HRL with learned subgoals; demonstrates that hierarchical temporal abstraction can improve sample efficiency when properly designed\\\\\\\"\\\\n  relevance_score: 3\\\\n\\\\n# ============================================================\\\\n# NEW: Action repeat / frame skip\\\\n# ============================================================\\\\n\\\\n- paper_id: braylan2015frame\\\\n  title: \\\\\\\"Frame Skip Is a Powerful Parameter for Learning to Play Atari\\\\\\\"\\\\n  authors: [Braylan A., Hollenbeck M., Meyerson E., Miikkulainen R.]\\\\n  year: 2015\\\\n  venue: \\\\\\\"AAAI Workshop on Learning for General Competency in Video Games\\\\\\\"\\\\n  category: background\\\\n  role: \\\\\\\"Empirical study showing frame skip strongly affects Atari performance; motivates investigation of temporal granularity as a critical design choice\\\\\\\"\\\\n  relevance_score: 3\\\\n\\\\n- paper_id: lakshminarayanan2017dynamic\\\\n  title: \\\\\\\"Dynamic Action Repetition for Deep Reinforcement Learning\\\\\\\"\\\\n  authors: [Lakshminarayanan A.S., Sharma S., Ravindran B.]\\\\n  year: 2017\\\\n  venue: AAAI\\\\n  category: method-component\\\\n  role: \\\\\\\"Learns per-step action repetition duration; model-free analog of our variable-dt imagination approach\\\\\\\"\\\\n  relevance_score: 4\\\\n\\\\n- paper_id: biedenkapp2021temporl\\\\n  title: \\\\\\\"TempoRL: Learning When to Act\\\\\\\"\\\\n  authors: [Biedenkapp A., Rajan R., Hutter F., Lindauer M.]\\\\n  year: 2021\\\\n  venue: ICML\\\\n  category: method-component\\\\n  role: \\\\\\\"Learns action persistence via skip-policy; demonstrates up to 10x speedup — but in model-free setting without the model exploitation risk we identify\\\\\\\"\\\\n  relevance_score: 4\\\\n\\\\n# ============================================================\\\\n# NEW: DreamerV2\\\\n# ============================================================\\\\n\\\\n- paper_id: hafner2021dreamerv2\\\\n  title: \\\\\\\"Mastering Atari with Discrete World Models\\\\\\\"\\\\n  authors: [Hafner D., Lillicrap T., Norouzi M., Ba J.]\\\\n  year: 2021\\\\n  venue: ICLR\\\\n  category: background\\\\n  role: \\\\\\\"DreamerV2 — introduces discrete latent representations used in DreamerV3; key architectural predecessor to our base system\\\\\\\"\\\\n  relevance_score: 5\\\\n\\\\n# ============================================================\\\\n# NEW: Alternative world model architectures\\\\n# ============================================================\\\\n\\\\n- paper_id: micheli2023iris\\\\n  title: \\\\\\\"Transformers are Sample-Efficient World Models\\\\\\\"\\\\n  authors: [Micheli V., Alonso E., Fleuret F.]\\\\n  year: 2023\\\\n  venue: ICLR\\\\n  category: background\\\\n  role: \\\\\\\"IRIS — autoregressive transformer world model; alternative to RSSM that may exhibit different compounding error characteristics under temporal abstraction\\\\\\\"\\\\n  relevance_score: 3\\\\n\\\\n- paper_id: robine2023twm\\\\n  title: \\\\\\\"Transformer-based World Models Are Happy With 100k Interactions\\\\\\\"\\\\n  authors: [Robine J., Hoeftmann M., Uelwer T., Harmeling S.]\\\\n  year: 2023\\\\n  venue: ICLR\\\\n  category: background\\\\n  role: \\\\\\\"TWM — Transformer-XL world model with direct state access; circumvents RSSM's recurrent compression that exacerbates our identified prediction gap\\\\\\\"\\\\n  relevance_score: 3\\\\n\\\\n- paper_id: chen2022transdreamer\\\\n  title: \\\\\\\"TransDreamer: Reinforcement Learning with Transformer World Models\\\\\\\"\\\\n  authors: [Chen C., Wu Y.-F., Yoon J., Ahn S.]\\\\n  year: 2022\\\\n  venue: \\\\\\\"arXiv:2202.09481\\\\\\\"\\\\n  category: background\\\\n  role: \\\\\\\"Replaces RSSM with Transformer State-Space Model; directly tests whether RSSM-specific architecture contributes to temporal abstraction failures\\\\\\\"\\\\n  relevance_score: 3\\\\n\\\\n# ============================================================\\\\n# NEW: 2024-2026 concurrent work on temporal abstraction in world models\\\\n# ============================================================\\\\n\\\\n- paper_id: gumbsch2024thick\\\\n  title: \\\\\\\"Learning Hierarchical World Models with Adaptive Temporal Abstractions from Discrete Latent Dynamics\\\\\\\"\\\\n  authors: [Gumbsch C., Sajid N., Martius G., Butz M.V.]\\\\n  year: 2024\\\\n  venue: ICLR\\\\n  category: direct-competitor\\\\n  role: \\\\\\\"THICK — learns adaptive temporal abstractions via context-change detection; closest concurrent work — addresses temporal abstraction in Dreamer but via hierarchy rather than variable-dt imagination\\\\\\\"\\\\n  relevance_score: 5\\\\n\\\\n- paper_id: mattes2024hieros\\\\n  title: \\\\\\\"Hieros: Hierarchical Imagination on Structured State Space Sequence World Models\\\\\\\"\\\\n  authors: [Mattes P., Schlosser R., Herbrich R.]\\\\n  year: 2024\\\\n  venue: ICML\\\\n  category: direct-competitor\\\\n  role: \\\\\\\"Multi-scale hierarchical imagination with S5 world model; demonstrates temporal abstraction via hierarchy avoids the single-scale dt-embedding failure we identify\\\\\\\"\\\\n  relevance_score: 5\\\\n\\\\n# ============================================================\\\\n# NEW: Seed-dependent instability & value overestimation in MBRL\\\\n# ============================================================\\\\n\\\\n- paper_id: henderson2018deep\\\\n  title: \\\\\\\"Deep Reinforcement Learning that Matters\\\\\\\"\\\\n  authors: [Henderson P., Islam R., Bachman P., Pineau J., Precup D., Meger D.]\\\\n  year: 2018\\\\n  venue: AAAI\\\\n  category: background\\\\n  role: \\\\\\\"Foundational study on seed variance in deep RL — shows statistically different performance distributions arise from random seeds alone with identical hyperparameters; directly supports our observation that seed 0 vs seed 2 produce qualitatively different value dynamics under the same dt_embed_dim=0 config\\\\\\\"\\\\n  relevance_score: 4\\\\n\\\\n- paper_id: nikishin2022primacy\\\\n  title: \\\\\\\"The Primacy Bias in Deep Reinforcement Learning\\\\\\\"\\\\n  authors: [Nikishin E., Schwarzer M., D'Oro P., Bacon P.-L., Courville A.]\\\\n  year: 2022\\\\n  venue: ICML\\\\n  category: background\\\\n  role: \\\\\\\"Identifies primacy bias — agents overfit early data and lose ability to learn from new transitions, leading to delayed performance collapse; parallels our finding where value overestimation initially appears benign but becomes pathological later, and the collapse timing is seed-dependent\\\\\\\"\\\\n  relevance_score: 4\\\\n\\\\n- paper_id: qiao2023mind\\\\n  title: \\\\\\\"Mind the Model, Not the Agent: The Primacy Bias in Model-based RL\\\\\\\"\\\\n  authors: [Qiao Z., Lyu J., Li X.]\\\\n  year: 2023\\\\n  venue: \\\\\\\"arXiv:2310.15017 (ECAI 2024)\\\\\\\"\\\\n  category: evaluation\\\\n  role: \\\\\\\"Extends primacy bias to MBRL, testing on DreamerV2 — shows world model primacy bias dominates over agent primacy bias; directly relevant to Dreamer-family training instability and explains why some seeds recover (model escapes early overfitting) while others don't\\\\\\\"\\\\n  relevance_score: 5\\\\n\\\\n- paper_id: hussing2024dissecting\\\\n  title: \\\\\\\"Dissecting Deep RL with High Update Ratios: Combatting Value Divergence\\\\\\\"\\\\n  authors: [Hussing M., Voelcker C.A., Gilitschenski I., Farahmand A.-M., Eaton E.]\\\\n  year: 2024\\\\n  venue: \\\\\\\"Reinforcement Learning Journal (RLC 2024)\\\\\\\"\\\\n  category: evaluation\\\\n  role: \\\\\\\"Shows value overestimation and Q-divergence under high update-to-data ratios, driven by optimizer momentum — overestimation occurs on both in-distribution and OOD data; mechanism maps to our CIVO where imagination-trained critic inflates values progressively, with divergence onset sensitive to initialization\\\\\\\"\\\\n  relevance_score: 4\\\\n\\\\n- paper_id: barkley2024stealing\\\\n  title: \\\\\\\"Stealing That Free Lunch: Exposing the Limits of Dyna-Style Reinforcement Learning\\\\\\\"\\\\n  authors: [Barkley B., Fridovich-Keil D.]\\\\n  year: 2024\\\\n  venue: \\\\\\\"arXiv:2412.14312 (ICML 2025)\\\\\\\"\\\\n  category: evaluation\\\\n  role: \\\\\\\"Demonstrates that synthetic rollouts (imagination) can degrade performance inconsistently across environments, with overestimation bias as a contributing factor; supports our finding that imagination-based training creates environment- and seed-dependent failure modes that existing mitigation techniques do not reliably fix\\\\\\\"\\\\n  relevance_score: 3\\\\n\\\\n- paper_id: bjorck2022variance\\\\n  title: \\\\\\\"Is High Variance Unavoidable in RL? A Case Study in Continuous Control\\\\\\\"\\\\n  authors: [Bjorck J., Gomes C.P., Weinberger K.Q.]\\\\n  year: 2022\\\\n  venue: ICLR\\\\n  category: background\\\\n  role: \\\\\\\"Shows RL variance mostly arises early in training from poor 'outlier' runs caused by numerical instability; parallels our observation that seed 2 diverges early while seed 0 recovers — the reward prediction degradation from removing dt_embedding may create exactly this early-training instability\\\\\\\"\\\\n  relevance_score: 3\\\\n\\\\n# ============================================================\\\\n# NEW: Reward prediction quality → MBRL performance\\\\n# ============================================================\\\\n# Our key finding: removing dt_embedding causes reward_MAE to spike 75x\\\\n# (0.01 → 0.747), making performance seed-dependent. These papers\\\\n# establish that reward prediction quality is a known MBRL bottleneck.\\\\n\\\\n- paper_id: lee2024dreamsmooth\\\\n  title: \\\\\\\"DreamSmooth: Improving Model-based Reinforcement Learning via Reward Smoothing\\\\\\\"\\\\n  authors: [Lee V., Abbeel P., Lee Y.]\\\\n  year: 2024\\\\n  venue: ICLR\\\\n  category: background\\\\n  role: \\\\\\\"Directly demonstrates reward prediction is a bottleneck in MBRL — sparse/ambiguous rewards cause the reward model to predict zeros, creating gradient-free landscapes during imagination; our dt_embed_dim=0 ablation creates an analogous bottleneck where the reward head loses temporal conditioning and MAE spikes 75x\\\\\\\"\\\\n  relevance_score: 5\\\\n\\\\n- paper_id: ma2024harmonydream\\\\n  title: \\\\\\\"HarmonyDream: Task Harmonization Inside World Models\\\\\\\"\\\\n  authors: [Ma H., Wu J., Feng N., Xiao C., Li D., Hao J., Wang J., Long M.]\\\\n  year: 2024\\\\n  venue: ICML\\\\n  category: background\\\\n  role: \\\\\\\"Shows observation prediction dominates reward prediction in world model training, degrading reward model quality; proposes dynamic loss balancing for 10-69% gains — directly relevant to our finding that dt_embedding removal disrupts the observation-reward prediction balance and causes reward MAE explosion\\\\\\\"\\\\n  relevance_score: 5\\\\n\\\\n- paper_id: lambert2020objective\\\\n  title: \\\\\\\"Objective Mismatch in Model-based Reinforcement Learning\\\\\\\"\\\\n  authors: [Lambert N., Amos B., Yadan O., Calandra R.]\\\\n  year: 2020\\\\n  venue: \\\\\\\"L4DC (Proceedings of Machine Learning Research, vol. 120)\\\\\\\"\\\\n  category: background\\\\n  role: \\\\\\\"Formalizes that one-step prediction likelihood does not correlate with control performance — the 'objective mismatch' problem; our work reveals a specific instance: the reward head's prediction accuracy (measured by MAE) directly gates whether the critic can learn stable value estimates, creating a reward-specific objective mismatch\\\\\\\"\\\\n  relevance_score: 4\\\\n\\\\n# ============================================================\\\\n# NEW: Auxiliary tasks & representation coupling in world models\\\\n# ============================================================\\\\n# Our finding: reward prediction quality is tightly coupled to temporal\\\\n# conditioning (dt_embedding). Removing the embedding degrades the\\\\n# reward head while dynamics remain intact — suggesting the reward head\\\\n# acts as more than a passive predictor; it conditions the shared\\\\n# representation. Literature gap: no prior work studies this coupling\\\\n# specifically in Dreamer-family world models.\\\\n\\\\n- paper_id: jaderberg2017unreal\\\\n  title: \\\\\\\"Reinforcement Learning with Unsupervised Auxiliary Tasks\\\\\\\"\\\\n  authors: [Jaderberg M., Mnih V., Czarnecki W.M., Schaul T., Leibo J.Z., Silver D., Kavukcuoglu K.]\\\\n  year: 2017\\\\n  venue: ICLR\\\\n  category: background\\\\n  role: \\\\\\\"UNREAL — introduces reward prediction as an auxiliary task that shapes shared representations; foundational evidence that reward prediction is not just a passive output but actively conditions what features the network learns — our finding that removing dt_embedding selectively degrades reward prediction (but not dynamics) suggests the temporal conditioning specifically enables reward-relevant feature extraction\\\\\\\"\\\\n  relevance_score: 4\\\\n\\\\n- paper_id: lyle2021auxiliary\\\\n  title: \\\\\\\"On The Effect of Auxiliary Tasks on Representation Dynamics\\\\\\\"\\\\n  authors: [Lyle C., Rowland M., Ostrovski G., Dabney W.]\\\\n  year: 2021\\\\n  venue: AISTATS\\\\n  category: background\\\\n  role: \\\\\\\"Theoretical analysis showing auxiliary tasks shape representations toward top eigenvectors of the transition operator; provides formal grounding for why removing temporal conditioning from the reward head could alter the entire representation — the reward head's gradients contribute to spectral structure of the shared latent space\\\\\\\"\\\\n  relevance_score: 4\\\\n\\\\n# ============================================================\\\\n# NEW: DreamerV3 architecture improvements (2025-2026)\\\\n# ============================================================\\\\n\\\\n- paper_id: bredis2026nedreamer\\\\n  title: \\\\\\\"Next Embedding Prediction Makes World Models Stronger\\\\\\\"\\\\n  authors: [Bredis G., Balagansky N., Gavrilov D., Rakhimov R.]\\\\n  year: 2026\\\\n  venue: \\\\\\\"arXiv:2603.02765\\\\\\\"\\\\n  category: background\\\\n  role: \\\\\\\"NE-Dreamer — decoder-free MBRL replacing pixel reconstruction with next-embedding prediction via temporal transformer + Barlow Twins; improves RSSM prediction quality on DMC and DMLab but does not address temporal abstraction or CIVO — orthogonal to our dt-embedding diagnosis\\\\\\\"\\\\n  relevance_score: 3\\\\n\\\\n- paper_id: zhang2025dymodreamer\\\\n  title: \\\\\\\"DyMoDreamer: World Modeling with Dynamic Modulation\\\\\\\"\\\\n  authors: [Zhang B., Wang R., Xiao W., Zhang W., Sun J., Huang G., Chen J., Wang G.]\\\\n  year: 2025\\\\n  venue: NeurIPS\\\\n  category: background\\\\n  role: \\\\\\\"Modulates RSSM via inter-frame differencing mask and stochastic categorical dynamic modulation; SOTA on Atari 100k (156.6% HNS) and DMC (832) — improves dynamics extraction but does not address variable-rate imagination or dt_embedding-induced value overestimation\\\\\\\"\\\\n  relevance_score: 3\\\\n\\\\n# ============================================================\\\\n# NEW: Temporal abstraction methods\\\\n# ============================================================\\\\n\\\\n- paper_id: liu2025vanta\\\\n  title: \\\\\\\"Semantic Temporal Abstraction via Vision-Language Model Guidance for Efficient Reinforcement Learning\\\\\\\"\\\\n  authors: [Liu T.-S., Liu X.-H., Chen R., Jin L., Wang P., Zhang Z., Yu Y.]\\\\n  year: 2025\\\\n  venue: ICLR\\\\n  category: method-component\\\\n  role: \\\\\\\"VanTA — VLM-guided trajectory decomposition into semantically meaningful skills via vector quantization + relabeling; operates at high-level skill abstraction (Franka Kitchen, Crafter) — contrasts with our low-level dt-based temporal abstraction within world-model imagination steps\\\\\\\"\\\\n  relevance_score: 3\\\\n\\\\n# ============================================================\\\\n# NEW: Evaluation methodology\\\\n# ============================================================\\\\n\\\\n- paper_id: agarwal2021precipice\\\\n  title: \\\\\\\"Deep Reinforcement Learning at the Edge of the Statistical Precipice\\\\\\\"\\\\n  authors: [Agarwal R., Schwarzer M., Castro P.S., Courville A.C., Bellemare M.]\\\\n  year: 2021\\\\n  venue: NeurIPS\\\\n  category: evaluation\\\\n  role: \\\\\\\"Proposes rliable — interval estimates, performance profiles, IQM for robust multi-seed RL evaluation (NeurIPS Outstanding Paper); our multi-seed experiment design follows this methodology to ensure statistical validity of collapse detection across seeds\\\\\\\"\\\\n  relevance_score: 4\\\\n\\\\n# ============================================================\\\\n# NEW (2026-05-14 gap analysis): Time discretization theory\\\\n# ============================================================\\\\n# Gap: variable timestep / time discretization invariance — foundational\\\\n# theory for why dt matters and how to handle it.\\\\n\\\\n- paper_id: tallec2019making\\\\n  title: \\\\\\\"Making Deep Q-learning methods Robust to Time Discretization\\\\\\\"\\\\n  authors: [Tallec C., Blier L., Ollivier Y.]\\\\n  year: 2019\\\\n  venue: \\\\\\\"ICML (arXiv:1901.09732)\\\\\\\"\\\\n  category: background\\\\n  role: \\\\\\\"Shows Q-learning performance is highly sensitive to time discretization δ; proposes architectural + exploration modifications for δ-invariance. Theoretical foundation for why our variable-dt imagination introduces a fundamental difficulty: RSSM trained at δ=1 cannot produce δ-invariant predictions at dt>1\\\\\\\"\\\\n  relevance_score: 4\\\\n\\\\n- paper_id: park2021sar\\\\n  title: \\\\\\\"Time Discretization-Invariant Safe Action Repetition for Policy Gradient Methods\\\\\\\"\\\\n  authors: [Park S., Kim J., Kim G.]\\\\n  year: 2021\\\\n  venue: \\\\\\\"NeurIPS (arXiv:2111.03941)\\\\\\\"\\\\n  category: method-component\\\\n  role: \\\\\\\"SAR — δ-invariant action repetition for policy gradients; achieves time-discretization robustness in model-free RL via adaptive reaction to state changes during repetition. Contrasts with our finding that world-model RL lacks this robustness when imagination uses dt>1\\\\\\\"\\\\n  relevance_score: 4\\\\n\\\\n- paper_id: wang2024seac\\\\n  title: \\\\\\\"Reinforcement Learning with Elastic Time Steps\\\\\\\"\\\\n  authors: [Wang D., Beltrame G.]\\\\n  year: 2024\\\\n  venue: \\\\\\\"arXiv:2402.14961\\\\\\\"\\\\n  category: method-component\\\\n  role: \\\\\\\"SEAC/MOSEAC — variable-duration time steps where agent selects both action and duration; model-free approach that explicitly treats action duration as part of the action space. Our work reveals why this strategy is problematic in world-model RL: the critic cannot reliably evaluate variable-duration imagined trajectories\\\\\\\"\\\\n  relevance_score: 3\\\\n\\\\n# ============================================================\\\\n# NEW (2026-05-14 gap analysis): Delusional bias mitigation\\\\n# ============================================================\\\\n\\\\n- paper_id: su2020conqur\\\\n  title: \\\\\\\"ConQUR: Mitigating Delusional Bias in Deep Q-learning\\\\\\\"\\\\n  authors: [Su D., Ooi J., Lu T., Schuurmans D., Boutilier C.]\\\\n  year: 2020\\\\n  venue: \\\\\\\"ICML (arXiv:2002.12399)\\\\\\\"\\\\n  category: background\\\\n  role: \\\\\\\"Follow-up to Lu et al. 2018; mitigates delusional bias via consistency-penalized Q-labels. Addresses delusional bias from policy-class constraints in Q-learning; our CIVO is an analogous phenomenon in MBRL where temporal conditioning (dt_embedding) creates inconsistent value targets across imagination steps\\\\\\\"\\\\n  relevance_score: 4\\\\n\\\\n# ============================================================\\\\n# NEW (2026-05-14 gap analysis): Diagnostic methodology in RL\\\\n# ============================================================\\\\n# Gap: our paper is a diagnostic analysis — need methodological\\\\n# precedents for \\\\\\\"what matters\\\\\\\" / \\\\\\\"implementation matters\\\\\\\" style papers.\\\\n\\\\n- paper_id: engstrom2020implementation\\\\n  title: \\\\\\\"Implementation Matters in Deep Policy Gradients: A Case Study on PPO and TRPO\\\\\\\"\\\\n  authors: [Engstrom L., Ilyas A., Santurkar S., Tsipras D., Janoos F., Rudolph L., Madry A.]\\\\n  year: 2020\\\\n  venue: \\\\\\\"ICLR (arXiv:2005.12729)\\\\\\\"\\\\n  category: evaluation\\\\n  role: \\\\\\\"Demonstrates that code-level implementation details (not algorithmic innovations) drive most of PPO's gains over TRPO; methodological precedent for our diagnostic approach — we similarly show that a specific implementation choice (trained vs. untrained dt_embedding) is the primary factor determining collapse vs. stability\\\\\\\"\\\\n  relevance_score: 4\\\\n\\\\n- paper_id: andrychowicz2021whatmatters\\\\n  title: \\\\\\\"What Matters for On-Policy Deep Actor-Critic Methods? A Large-Scale Study\\\\\\\"\\\\n  authors: [Andrychowicz M., Raichuk A., Stańczyk P., Orsini M., Girgin S., Marinier R., Hussenot L., Geist M., Pietquin O., Michalski M., Gelly S., Bachem O.]\\\\n  year: 2021\\\\n  venue: \\\\\\\"ICLR (arXiv:2006.05990)\\\\\\\"\\\\n  category: evaluation\\\\n  role: \\\\\\\"Large-scale factorial study of 50+ design choices in on-policy RL (250K+ agents); methodological template for our factorial experiment design isolating dt_embedding × subsample × horizon effects. Demonstrates that systematic ablation reveals non-obvious interactions — parallel to our finding that dt_embedding training status interacts with subsample and horizon\\\\\\\"\\\\n  relevance_score: 4\\\\n\\\\n# ============================================================\\\\n# NEW (2026-05-14 gap analysis): MBRL rollout quality & value overestimation\\\\n# ============================================================\\\\n# Gap: recent ICLR 2025 papers directly studying imagination rollout\\\\n# quality and value overestimation in model-based settings.\\\\n\\\\n- paper_id: frauenknecht2025rollouts\\\\n  title: \\\\\\\"On Rollouts in Model-Based Reinforcement Learning\\\\\\\"\\\\n  authors: [Frauenknecht B., Subhasish D., Solowjow F., Trimpe S.]\\\\n  year: 2025\\\\n  venue: \\\\\\\"ICLR (arXiv:2501.16918)\\\\\\\"\\\\n  category: evaluation\\\\n  role: \\\\\\\"Shows trajectory-sampling rollouts diverge from ground truth after few steps and can harm policy learning; proposes Infoprop separating aleatoric/epistemic uncertainty with rollout termination criteria. Directly supports our finding that dt>1 imagination produces corrupted data — our work identifies a specific mechanism (dt_embedding-induced value exploitation) beyond general compounding error\\\\\\\"\\\\n  relevance_score: 5\\\\n\\\\n- paper_id: voelcker2025madtd\\\\n  title: \\\\\\\"MAD-TD: Model-Augmented Data stabilizes High Update Ratio RL\\\\\\\"\\\\n  authors: [Voelcker C., Hussing M., Eaton E., Farahmand A.-M., Gilitschenski I.]\\\\n  year: 2025\\\\n  venue: \\\\\\\"ICLR (arXiv:2410.08896)\\\\\\\"\\\\n  category: evaluation\\\\n  role: \\\\\\\"Shows value function misgeneralization to on-policy actions causes instability at high UTD ratios; uses model-generated data to improve value accuracy. Complementary to our finding: MAD-TD addresses value misgeneralization from replay distribution mismatch, we address value overestimation from temporal conditioning corruption in imagination\\\\\\\"\\\\n  relevance_score: 4\\\\n\\\\n# ============================================================\\\\n# NEW (2026-05-14 gap analysis): Latest action repeat methods\\\\n# ============================================================\\\\n\\\\n- paper_id: nie2025sdar\\\\n  title: \\\\\\\"Select before Act: Spatially Decoupled Action Repetition for Continuous Control\\\\\\\"\\\\n  authors: [Nie B., et al.]\\\\n  year: 2025\\\\n  venue: \\\\\\\"ICLR (arXiv:2502.06919)\\\\\\\"\\\\n  category: method-component\\\\n  role: \\\\\\\"SDAR — per-dimension action repetition decisions for flexible temporal persistence in model-free RL; SOTA on DMC continuous control. Advances action repeat in model-free setting; our work shows the fundamental obstacle to analogous variable-rate approaches in model-based RL (CIVO from dt_embedding)\\\\\\\"\\\\n  relevance_score: 3\\\\n\\\\n# ============================================================\\\\n# NEW (2026-05-14 gap analysis): DreamerV4 / latest Dreamer evolution\\\\n# ============================================================\\\\n\\\\n- paper_id: hafner2025dreamerv4\\\\n  title: \\\\\\\"Training Agents Inside of Scalable World Models\\\\\\\"\\\\n  authors: [Hafner D., Yan W., Lillicrap T.]\\\\n  year: 2025\\\\n  venue: \\\\\\\"arXiv:2509.24527\\\\\\\"\\\\n  category: background\\\\n  role: \\\\\\\"DreamerV4 — replaces RSSM with efficient transformer world model + shortcut forcing; scales to video pretraining (Minecraft diamonds from video). Architectural successor to DreamerV3; our dt_embedding diagnosis is specific to RSSM but the broader lesson (temporal conditioning must match model fidelity) applies to transformer world models\\\\\\\"\\\\n  relevance_score: 4\\\\n\\\\n# ============================================================\\\\n# NEW (2026-05-14): Training instability dynamics\\\\n# ============================================================\\\\n\\\\n- paper_id: zhang2026instability\\\\n  title: \\\\\\\"Training instability in deep learning follows low-dimensional dynamical principles\\\\\\\"\\\\n  authors: [Zhang L., et al.]\\\\n  year: 2026\\\\n  venue: \\\\\\\"ICLR 2026 (arXiv:2601.13160)\\\\\\\"\\\\n  category: background\\\\n  role: \\\\\\\"Training instability follows low-dimensional dynamical principles; provides theoretical framework for why seed-dependent collapse vs self-correction occurs in our experiments (008d seed 1 collapses, 009b seed 2 self-corrects under identical config)\\\\\\\"\\\\n  relevance_score: 5\\\\n\\\\n# ============================================================\\\\n# NEW (2026-05-14): Seed-Dependent Stochastic Outcomes in MBRL\\\\n# ============================================================\\\\n# Dedicated literature survey for the stochastic collapse phenomenon:\\\\n# same config (trained dt_embedding + subsample + H=8) produces\\\\n# collapse in seed 0 (008d) but self-correction in seed 2 (009b).\\\\n# nve>1.5x is a 100% reliable marker of trained dt_embedding,\\\\n# but collapse itself is stochastic (1/2 seeds).\\\\n\\\\n- paper_id: sokar2023dormant\\\\n  title: \\\\\\\"The Dormant Neuron Phenomenon in Deep Reinforcement Learning\\\\\\\"\\\\n  authors: [Sokar G., Agarwal R., Castro P.S., Evci U.]\\\\n  year: 2023\\\\n  venue: \\\\\\\"ICML 2023\\\\\\\"\\\\n  category: background\\\\n  role: \\\\\\\"Identifies dormant neurons — inactive units accumulating during RL training that reduce network expressivity. Seed-dependent because different random initializations produce different early dormancy patterns; directly explains why some seeds lose the representational capacity needed to self-correct value overestimation (our seed 0 collapses) while others retain enough active neurons to recover (our seed 2 self-corrects)\\\\\\\"\\\\n  relevance_score: 4\\\\n  survey_tag: seed-dependent-stochastic-outcomes\\\\n\\\\n- paper_id: lyle2022capacity\\\\n  title: \\\\\\\"Understanding and Preventing Capacity Loss in Reinforcement Learning\\\\\\\"\\\\n  authors: [Lyle C., Rowland M., Dabney W.]\\\\n  year: 2022\\\\n  venue: \\\\\\\"ICLR 2023 (arXiv:2204.09560)\\\\\\\"\\\\n  category: background\\\\n  role: \\\\\\\"Shows feature rank collapse from non-stationary TD targets is a necessary condition for learning failure but not sufficient — sparse rewards and other factors must co-occur. Directly parallels our finding: nve>1.5x (value overestimation from trained dt_embedding) is a necessary precondition for collapse but not a sufficient one; additional stochastic factors (initialization, early replay composition) determine whether collapse actually occurs\\\\\\\"\\\\n  relevance_score: 5\\\\n  survey_tag: seed-dependent-stochastic-outcomes\\\\n\\\\n- paper_id: kumar2022dr3\\\\n  title: \\\\\\\"DR3: Value-Based Deep Reinforcement Learning Requires Explicit Regularization\\\\\\\"\\\\n  authors: [Kumar A., Agarwal R., Ma T., Courville A., Tucker G., Levine S.]\\\\n  year: 2022\\\\n  venue: \\\\\\\"ICLR 2022\\\\\\\"\\\\n  category: background\\\\n  role: \\\\\\\"Shows implicit regularization from TD learning favors degenerate feature aliasing (states on both sides of Bellman backup become indistinguishable), creating the substrate for value overestimation. In our setting, trained dt_embedding amplifies this aliasing across different temporal horizons — the critic cannot distinguish between dt=1 and dt>1 value targets, enabling exploitation. Feature aliasing is seed-dependent because it depends on initialization geometry\\\\\\\"\\\\n  relevance_score: 4\\\\n  survey_tag: seed-dependent-stochastic-outcomes\\\\n\\\\n- paper_id: colas2018seeds\\\\n  title: \\\\\\\"How Many Random Seeds? Statistical Power Analysis in Deep Reinforcement Learning Experiments\\\\\\\"\\\\n  authors: [Colas C., Sigaud O., Oudeyer P.-Y.]\\\\n  year: 2018\\\\n  venue: \\\\\\\"arXiv:1806.08295\\\\\\\"\\\\n  category: evaluation\\\\n  role: \\\\\\\"Provides statistical framework for determining seed count needed for significant algorithm comparison; our 2-seed observation (1/2 collapse) has limited statistical power by their analysis — but the qualitative difference (nve 4.12x vs 0.38x) is large enough that even 2 seeds establish the stochastic nature of the phenomenon. Methodological basis for future multi-seed validation\\\\\\\"\\\\n  relevance_score: 3\\\\n  survey_tag: seed-dependent-stochastic-outcomes\\\\n\\\\n- paper_id: nikishin2023plasticity\\\\n  title: \\\\\\\"Deep Reinforcement Learning with Plasticity Injection\\\\\\\"\\\\n  authors: [Nikishin E., Oh J., Ostrovski G., Lyle C., Pascanu R., Dabney W., Barreto A.]\\\\n  year: 2023\\\\n  venue: \\\\\\\"NeurIPS 2023\\\\\\\"\\\\n  category: method-component\\\\n  role: \\\\\\\"Plasticity injection augments network plasticity without changing parameter count; serves as a diagnostic tool — if injection improves performance, plasticity loss was the bottleneck. Directly applicable to diagnosing whether our seed-dependent collapse is plasticity-mediated: if plasticity injection prevents collapse in seed 0 but has no effect on seed 2 (which already self-corrects), it confirms plasticity loss as the bifurcation mechanism\\\\\\\"\\\\n  relevance_score: 4\\\\n  survey_tag: seed-dependent-stochastic-outcomes\\\\n\\\\n- paper_id: schwarzer2023bbf\\\\n  title: \\\\\\\"Bigger, Better, Faster: Human-level Atari with Human-level Efficiency\\\\\\\"\\\\n  authors: [Schwarzer M., Obando-Ceron J.S., Courville A., Bellemare M., Agarwal R., Castro P.S.]\\\\n  year: 2023\\\\n  venue: \\\\\\\"ICML 2023\\\\\\\"\\\\n  category: method-component\\\\n  role: \\\\\\\"BBF achieves SOTA sample efficiency via periodic network resets + scaling + weight decay; periodic resets prevent primacy bias accumulation across seeds. Suggests our CIVO collapse might be preventable with periodic critic resets — the reset would break the positive feedback loop between overestimated values and actor exploitation before it becomes irreversible\\\\\\\"\\\\n  relevance_score: 3\\\\n  survey_tag: seed-dependent-stochastic-outcomes\\\\n\\\\n- paper_id: farebrother2024stopregressing\\\\n  title: \\\\\\\"Stop Regressing: Training Value Functions via Classification for Scalable Deep RL\\\\\\\"\\\\n  authors: [Farebrother J., Orbay J., Vuong Q., Taiga A.A., Chebotar Y., Xiao T., Irpan A., Levine S., Castro P.S., Faust A., Kumar A., Agarwal R.]\\\\n  year: 2024\\\\n  venue: \\\\\\\"ICML 2024\\\\\\\"\\\\n  category: method-component\\\\n  role: \\\\\\\"Shows categorical cross-entropy for value training provides implicit regularization against overestimation vs MSE regression. DreamerV3 already uses categorical value prediction (twohot + symlog) — yet our trained dt_embedding still induces collapse in some seeds, demonstrating that categorical value training is insufficient to prevent dt_embedding-induced value exploitation\\\\\\\"\\\\n  relevance_score: 3\\\\n  survey_tag: seed-dependent-stochastic-outcomes\\\\n\\\\n- paper_id: lyle2024normalization\\\\n  title: \\\\\\\"Normalization and Effective Learning Rates in Reinforcement Learning\\\\\\\"\\\\n  authors: [Lyle C., Zheng Z., Giunchiglia E., Sherstan C., Hashemizadeh M., Schuurmans D., Dabney W.]\\\\n  year: 2024\\\\n  venue: \\\\\\\"NeurIPS 2024\\\\\\\"\\\\n  category: background\\\\n  role: \\\\\\\"Shows normalization layers combat overestimation but cause effective learning rate decay via parameter norm growth. Provides a potential mechanism for seed 2's self-correction: if parameter norms grow faster in certain initializations, effective LR decays faster, naturally damping value overestimation before it cascades into collapse. Seed 0's slower norm growth → sustained high effective LR → overestimation compounds → collapse\\\\\\\"\\\\n  relevance_score: 4\\\\n  survey_tag: seed-dependent-stochastic-outcomes\\\\n\\\\n# --- Survey synthesis: Seed-Dependent Stochastic Outcomes ---\\\\n# Summary (2026-05-14):\\\\n#\\\\n# 1. STOCHASTIC COLLAPSE HAS PRECEDENT:\\\\n#    Plasticity loss (Lyle 2022, Sokar 2023, Nikishin 2023) is inherently\\\\n#    seed-dependent because it depends on initialization → early gradient\\\\n#    dynamics → neuron activity patterns. Different seeds hit different\\\\n#    plasticity trajectories under identical configs.\\\\n#\\\\n# 2. nve>1.5x AS DIAGNOSTIC MARKER (necessary but not sufficient):\\\\n#    Lyle 2022 shows feature rank collapse is necessary but not sufficient\\\\n#    for learning failure. Kumar 2022 shows feature aliasing from TD\\\\n#    learning creates the overestimation substrate. Our nve>1.5x is\\\\n#    analogous: it indicates the dt_embedding has enabled value exploitation\\\\n#    (100% reliable marker), but collapse requires additional conditions\\\\n#    (plasticity loss, insufficient effective LR decay) that are stochastic.\\\\n#\\\\n# 3. SELF-CORRECTION MECHANISM:\\\\n#    Lyle 2024 provides a candidate mechanism: normalization-induced\\\\n#    effective LR decay can naturally damp overestimation in some seeds.\\\\n#    Farebrother 2024 shows categorical value training provides partial\\\\n#    implicit regularization. Together these explain why seed 2 self-corrects:\\\\n#    the combination of DreamerV3's categorical critic + normalization +\\\\n#    favorable initialization produces enough implicit regularization to\\\\n#    overcome the dt_embedding-induced overestimation.\\\\n#\\\\n# 4. THEORETICAL GROUNDING:\\\\n#    Zhang 2026 (already in map) provides the dynamical systems framework.\\\\n#    Bjorck 2022 (already in map) shows early outlier events dominate\\\\n#    variance. Together with the new papers, the framing is:\\\\n#    \\\\\\\"trained dt_embedding creates a necessary condition (nve>1.5x) for\\\\n#    CIVO collapse, but collapse is a stochastic bifurcation\\\\n#    whose outcome depends on seed-dependent plasticity dynamics.\\\\\\\"\\\\n\\\\n# ============================================================\\\\n# INCREMENTAL SCAN (2026-05-14): Δt conditioning & adaptive horizon\\\\n# ============================================================\\\\n# 8 new papers from targeted search on:\\\\n#   - Δt/timestep conditioning in world models\\\\n#   - Variable-rate imagination / adaptive horizon\\\\n#   - Hierarchical planning with latent world models (2025-2026)\\\\n#\\\\n# KEY FINDING: TAWM (Nhu et al. ICML 2025) explicitly conditions\\\\n# world model on Δt — closest methodological overlap. But TAWM\\\\n# uses TD-MPC2 (online MPC) not imagination-based actor-critic,\\\\n# and treats Δt conditioning as beneficial. Our work diagnoses\\\\n# Δt conditioning as pathological in imagination-based training\\\\n# (CIVO). Complementary, not duplicative.\\\\n\\\\n- paper_id: nhu2025tawm\\\\n  title: \\\\\\\"Time-Aware World Model for Adaptive Prediction and Control\\\\\\\"\\\\n  authors: [Nhu A.N., Son S., Lin M.C.]\\\\n  year: 2025\\\\n  venue: \\\\\\\"ICML 2025 (arXiv:2506.08441)\\\\\\\"\\\\n  category: direct-competitor\\\\n  role: \\\\\\\"TAWM — explicitly conditions world model on time-step size Δt and trains over diverse Δt values for multi-rate dynamics learning. Built on TD-MPC2 (online MPC). KEY DISTINCTION from our work: (1) TAWM treats Δt conditioning as beneficial for performance/data-efficiency; we diagnose it as pathological in imagination-based actor-critic training (CIVO). (2) TAWM uses MPC (no imagination rollouts for policy training); our failure mode is specific to imagination-based training where the critic exploits dt-conditioned value estimates. (3) TAWM focuses on observation-rate robustness; we focus on value overestimation from temporal conditioning corruption. TAWM actually strengthens our contribution: it shows Δt conditioning works in MPC settings, making our finding that it fails in imagination-based settings a surprising and important diagnostic.\\\\\\\"\\\\n  relevance_score: 5\\\\n  novelty_threat: \\\\\\\"MEDIUM — methodological overlap (Δt conditioning) but fundamentally different paradigm (MPC vs imagination) and opposite conclusion (beneficial vs pathological). Must cite and differentiate in paper.\\\\\\\"\\\\n\\\\n- paper_id: li2025lsimagine\\\\n  title: \\\\\\\"Open-World Reinforcement Learning over Long Short-Term Imagination\\\\\\\"\\\\n  authors: [Li J., Wang Q., Wang Y., Jin X., Li Y., Zeng W., Yang X.]\\\\n  year: 2025\\\\n  venue: \\\\\\\"ICLR 2025 Oral (arXiv:2410.03618)\\\\\\\"\\\\n  category: direct-competitor\\\\n  role: \\\\\\\"LS-Imagine — extends imagination horizon in Dreamer via goal-conditioned jumpy state transitions and affordance maps. Addresses the 'short-sightedness' of standard Dreamer imagination. KEY DISTINCTION: LS-Imagine adds jumpy transitions to reach long-horizon targets (open-world Minecraft), while our work shows that variable-dt imagination itself introduces CIVO. LS-Imagine's jumpy transitions use goal conditioning (not dt-embedding), potentially avoiding the value overestimation we identify.\\\\\\\"\\\\n  relevance_score: 4\\\\n  novelty_threat: \\\\\\\"LOW — different mechanism (goal-conditioned jumps vs dt-embedding) and different focus (long-horizon exploration vs diagnostic of failure modes). Should cite as concurrent approach to extending imagination horizon.\\\\\\\"\\\\n\\\\n- paper_id: zhang2026hwm\\\\n  title: \\\\\\\"Hierarchical Planning with Latent World Models\\\\\\\"\\\\n  authors: [Zhang W., Terver B., Zholus A., Chitnis S., Sutaria H., Assran M., Balestriero R., Bar A., Bardes A., LeCun Y., Ballas N.]\\\\n  year: 2026\\\\n  venue: \\\\\\\"arXiv:2604.03208\\\\\\\"\\\\n  category: direct-competitor\\\\n  role: \\\\\\\"HWM — learns multi-scale latent world models for hierarchical MPC planning; high-level planner optimizes macro-actions, low-level planner handles primitives. 70% success on real-world non-greedy robotic tasks vs 0% for single-level. Addresses temporal abstraction via hierarchical planning (MPC), not imagination-based actor-critic. Further evidence that temporal abstraction in world models requires hierarchy rather than single-scale variable-dt approaches.\\\\\\\"\\\\n  relevance_score: 4\\\\n  novelty_threat: \\\\\\\"LOW — MPC-based hierarchical planning, not imagination-based training. Supports our thesis that flat dt-embedding approaches are inferior to hierarchical alternatives.\\\\\\\"\\\\n\\\\n- paper_id: kobayashi2025metacontroller\\\\n  title: \\\\\\\"Emergent temporal abstractions in autoregressive models enable hierarchical reinforcement learning\\\\\\\"\\\\n  authors: [Kobayashi S., et al.]\\\\n  year: 2025\\\\n  venue: \\\\\\\"arXiv:2512.20605\\\\\\\"\\\\n  category: method-component\\\\n  role: \\\\\\\"MetaController — discovers temporal abstractions via higher-order non-causal sequence model controlling base autoregressive model's residual stream. Each controller executes behaviorally meaningful action sequences with learned termination conditions. Operates in fundamentally different paradigm (LLM-style autoregressive models, not world-model imagination), but demonstrates that temporal abstraction benefits from hierarchical structure rather than flat dt-conditioning.\\\\\\\"\\\\n  relevance_score: 3\\\\n\\\\n- paper_id: shaj2023mts3\\\\n  title: \\\\\\\"Multi Time Scale World Models\\\\\\\"\\\\n  authors: [Shaj V., Gholam Zadeh S., Demir O., Douat L.R., Neumann G.]\\\\n  year: 2023\\\\n  venue: \\\\\\\"NeurIPS 2023 (arXiv:2310.18534)\\\\\\\"\\\\n  category: method-component\\\\n  role: \\\\\\\"MTS3 — probabilistic multi-time-scale state space model with fast and slow latent dynamics for variable-rate prediction. Provides efficient inference across temporal scales. Foundational multi-rate dynamics architecture; our work shows that even with proper multi-rate modeling, the downstream actor-critic training in imagination can exploit temporal conditioning for value overestimation — a failure mode MTS3 does not address (it focuses on prediction quality, not policy training).\\\\\\\"\\\\n  relevance_score: 4\\\\n\\\\n- paper_id: splates2025\\\\n  title: \\\\\\\"Stable Planning with Temporally Extended Skills\\\\\\\"\\\\n  authors: [SPlaTES authors]\\\\n  year: 2025\\\\n  venue: \\\\\\\"Reinforcement Learning Journal (RLC 2025)\\\\\\\"\\\\n  category: method-component\\\\n  role: \\\\\\\"SPlaTES — hierarchical MPC with temporally extended skills + abstract skill world model. Skill learning via mutual-information objective yields diverse, predictable, task-related behavior. Demonstrates that stable long-horizon planning requires modeling skill outcomes (temporal abstraction via hierarchy), not primitive-action outcomes at variable time steps — consistent with our finding that flat dt-embedding fails.\\\\\\\"\\\\n  relevance_score: 3\\\\n\\\\n- paper_id: beckerehmck2023multitimestep\\\\n  title: \\\\\\\"Multi-timestep models for Model-based Reinforcement Learning\\\\\\\"\\\\n  authors: [Becker-Ehmck P., Peters J., van der Smagt P.]\\\\n  year: 2023\\\\n  venue: \\\\\\\"arXiv:2310.05672\\\\\\\"\\\\n  category: background\\\\n  role: \\\\\\\"Proposes multi-timestep training objective (weighted sum of losses at various future horizons) for one-step dynamics models to improve long-horizon R² score. Addresses compounding error at the model training level; our work shows that even with perfect multi-step prediction, the imagination-based actor-critic can still fail due to value overestimation from dt-conditioning — a downstream failure mode distinct from prediction accuracy.\\\\\\\"\\\\n  relevance_score: 3\\\\n\\\\n- paper_id: liu2022dmve\\\\n  title: \\\\\\\"Dynamic-Horizon Model-Based Value Estimation With Latent Imagination\\\\\\\"\\\\n  authors: [Liu Y., et al.]\\\\n  year: 2022\\\\n  venue: \\\\\\\"IEEE TNNLS (arXiv:2009.09593)\\\\\\\"\\\\n  category: background\\\\n  role: \\\\\\\"DMVE — adaptive rollout horizon selection via horizon reliability detection (comparing value expansion errors between raw and reconstructed observations). Addresses the horizon selection problem in imagination-based value estimation. Complementary to our work: DMVE selects among fixed-dt horizons; we show that even optimal horizon selection cannot fix the CIVO when dt-embedding is trained (the overestimation is in the value function, not the horizon length).\\\\\\\"\\\\n  relevance_score: 3\\\\n\\\\n# --- Incremental scan synthesis (2026-05-14) ---\\\\n#\\\\n# NOVELTY ASSESSMENT:\\\\n# No paper found that diagnoses dt_embedding → CIVO\\\\n# (value overestimation) → stochastic collapse in imagination-based\\\\n# MBRL. Our core contribution remains novel.\\\\n#\\\\n# TAWM (ICML 2025) is the closest methodological overlap but\\\\n# operates in MPC paradigm and reaches opposite conclusion\\\\n# (Δt conditioning is beneficial). This actually STRENGTHENS\\\\n# our novelty: \\\\\\\"Δt conditioning helps in MPC but hurts in\\\\n# imagination-based training\\\\\\\" is a more nuanced and surprising finding.\\\\n#\\\\n# LANDSCAPE TREND:\\\\n# The field is converging on HIERARCHY (THICK, Hieros, Director,\\\\n# HWM, SPlaTES, MetaController) as the solution to temporal\\\\n# abstraction in world models, avoiding flat variable-dt approaches.\\\\n# Our diagnostic paper explains WHY flat dt approaches fail,\\\\n# providing theoretical grounding for this empirical trend.\\\\n#\\\\n# ACTION ITEMS FOR PAPER:\\\\n# 1. MUST CITE: nhu2025tawm — differentiate MPC vs imagination paradigm\\\\n# 2. SHOULD CITE: li2025lsimagine — concurrent Dreamer horizon extension\\\\n# 3. SHOULD CITE: shaj2023mts3 — multi-rate dynamics foundation\\\\n# 4. CONSIDER: zhang2026hwm — latest hierarchical WM planning\\\\n\\\\n# ============================================================\\\\n# INCREMENTAL SCAN (2026-05-15): Value expansion horizon & overestimation\\\\n# ============================================================\\\\n# 4 new papers from targeted search on:\\\\n#   - \\\\\\\"temporal abstraction\\\\\\\" + \\\\\\\"world model\\\\\\\" + RL (2024-2026)\\\\n#   - \\\\\\\"CIVO\\\\\\\" / \\\\\\\"value overestimation\\\\\\\" + MBRL\\\\n#   - \\\\\\\"imagination horizon\\\\\\\" + world model\\\\n#   - \\\\\\\"value function collapse\\\\\\\" / \\\\\\\"value divergence\\\\\\\" + MBRL\\\\n#   - variable timestep imagination + actor-critic failure\\\\n#\\\\n# KEY FINDING: Still NO paper diagnosing dt_embedding → CIVO\\\\n# → stochastic collapse in imagination-based MBRL.\\\\n# Core contribution remains novel. Palenicek 2025 is the most\\\\n# relevant new addition — shows even oracle dynamics don't help\\\\n# with longer rollout horizons, supporting our thesis that the\\\\n# bottleneck is NOT model accuracy but value estimation corruption.\\\\n\\\\n- paper_id: palenicek2025diminishing\\\\n  title: \\\\\\\"Diminishing Return of Value Expansion Methods\\\\\\\"\\\\n  authors: [Palenicek D., Lutter M., Carvalho J., Dennert D., Ahmad F., Peters J.]\\\\n  year: 2025\\\\n  venue: \\\\\\\"Reinforcement Learning Journal (RLC 2025, arXiv:2412.20537)\\\\\\\"\\\\n  category: evaluation\\\\n  role: \\\\\\\"Shows longer model-based rollout horizons have diminishing returns in sample efficiency — even with oracle dynamics models, each additional expansion step yields progressively smaller gains. The bottleneck is NOT model accuracy. Directly supports our finding: extending imagination horizon via dt>1 does not improve performance because the problem lies in value estimation (CIVO from dt_embedding), not dynamics quality. Strengthens our argument that dt=1 imagination is sufficient.\\\\\\\"\\\\n  relevance_score: 5\\\\n\\\\n- paper_id: kim2025deas\\\\n  title: \\\\\\\"DEAS: DEtached value learning with Action Sequence for Scalable Offline RL\\\\\\\"\\\\n  authors: [Kim C., Seo Y., et al.]\\\\n  year: 2025\\\\n  venue: \\\\\\\"arXiv:2510.07730\\\\\\\"\\\\n  category: method-component\\\\n  role: \\\\\\\"Shows action sequences (temporal extension via options/semi-MDP) cause excessive value overestimation in actor-critic algorithms; proposes detached value learning where critic trains separately from policy. Parallel to our finding: temporal extension (whether via action sequences or dt-embedding) creates value overestimation in actor-critic; DEAS's detached learning is analogous to our dt=1 imagination fix (decoupling temporal abstraction from value estimation).\\\\\\\"\\\\n  relevance_score: 4\\\\n\\\\n- paper_id: luo2025vpl\\\\n  title: \\\\\\\"A Case for Validation Buffer in Pessimistic Actor-Critic\\\\\\\"\\\\n  authors: [Nauman M., Ostaszewski M., Cygan M.]\\\\n  year: 2025\\\\n  venue: \\\\\\\"IJCAI 2025 (arXiv:2403.01014)\\\\\\\"\\\\n  category: method-component\\\\n  role: \\\\\\\"Validation Pessimism Learning (VPL) — uses validation buffer to adaptively adjust pessimism levels throughout training; shows pessimism is beneficial only during overestimation, detrimental during underestimation. Relevant to our setting: our trained dt_embedding creates persistent overestimation (nve>1.5x), suggesting adaptive pessimism could be a complementary mitigation to our dt=1 imagination restriction.\\\\\\\"\\\\n  relevance_score: 3\\\\n\\\\n- paper_id: lenz2025macura\\\\n  title: \\\\\\\"Trust the Model Where It Trusts Itself -- Model-Based Actor-Critic with Uncertainty-Aware Rollout Adaption\\\\\\\"\\\\n  authors: [Lenz S., et al.]\\\\n  year: 2025\\\\n  venue: \\\\\\\"arXiv:2405.19014\\\\\\\"\\\\n  category: method-component\\\\n  role: \\\\\\\"MACURA — uses model uncertainty to adaptively determine local rollout length in model-based actor-critic; avoids uniform rollout horizon. Addresses rollout quality from the uncertainty perspective; our work identifies a different mechanism: even if the model is confident, dt-embedding-conditioned imagination can produce overestimated value estimates (CIVO). MACURA's uncertainty-based termination would not catch our failure mode because the model predictions may be accurate while value estimates are corrupted.\\\\\\\"\\\\n  relevance_score: 3\\\\n\\\\n# --- Incremental scan synthesis (2026-05-15) ---\\\\n#\\\\n# NOVELTY ASSESSMENT (confirmed):\\\\n# No paper found that diagnoses dt_embedding → CIVO\\\\n# (value overestimation) → stochastic collapse in imagination-based\\\\n# MBRL. Core contribution remains novel after 2nd scan.\\\\n#\\\\n# KEY NEW INSIGHT from Palenicek 2025:\\\\n# Even oracle dynamics models show diminishing returns with longer\\\\n# rollouts. This means the value estimation bottleneck (not model\\\\n# accuracy) is increasingly recognized as the fundamental limit\\\\n# of imagination-based MBRL — our paper explains a specific\\\\n# mechanism (dt_embedding-induced CIVO) by which\\\\n# this bottleneck manifests.\\\\n#\\\\n# DEAS (Kim 2025) provides independent evidence from offline RL\\\\n# that temporal extension (action sequences) → value overestimation\\\\n# in actor-critic. Different setting (offline vs online, action\\\\n# sequences vs dt-embedding) but same causal pattern.\\\\n#\\\\n# NO DIRECT COMPETITORS FOUND at CoRL 2025/2026.\\\\n#\\\\n# UPDATED ACTION ITEMS FOR PAPER:\\\\n# 1. MUST CITE: palenicek2025diminishing — rollout horizon diminishing\\\\n#    returns support our \\\\\\\"dt=1 is sufficient\\\\\\\" conclusion\\\\n# 2. SHOULD CITE: kim2025deas — independent evidence of temporal\\\\n#    extension → value overestimation in actor-critic\\\\n# 3. CONSIDER: luo2025vpl — adaptive pessimism as potential mitigation\\\\n\\\", \\\"total_chars\\\": 55491, \\\"truncated\\\": false}, \\\"error\\\": null, \\\"metadata\\\": {}}\"}"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_011ABPrh3guy35EGhbNGmkw9","session_id":"670b194d-bd1a-4414-88fd-4c7f9eb01a25","uuid":"91f050c2-089d-4067-8b69-8055cf11304b","timestamp":"2026-05-16T14:16:15.045Z"}
